{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat memdiag-reader-brief-memory.md'","aggregated_output":"# Gate 2 memory-thesis marks (read-only)\n\nYou are an independent reader. Read only this brief and the packet named in your instructions. Do not open other files or run commands or model calls.\n\nEach entry is one research question (question, outcome, period). Give each exactly one mark:\n- `one-year price`: a price level for one period;\n- `change`: the move from one year to another (a question that tracks a level and the change is marked change);\n- `span`: a price over several years without a change;\n- `not a price`: anything else.\n\nReturn one JSON object per entry, one per line, in packet order, and nothing else: `{\"n\": 1, \"mark\": \"...\", \"why\": \"one sentence\"}`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat memdiag-packet-memory.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat memdiag-packet-memory.json'","aggregated_output":"[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"question\": \"What will contract prices for the DRAM, LPDDR5X and NAND memory used in NVIDIA's AI racks average in calendar 2027 — the component cost that now makes up roughly a quarter to 30% of a Vera Rubin NVL72 rack's bill of materials and that the item says is supply-constrained?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The direction and magnitude of average DRAM/NAND contract prices for AI-rack memory in calendar 2027 versus 2026, as shown by market contract-price trackers and memory makers' reported prices and guidance.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 (the second year of the item's 'next two years' AI-capacity budgeting horizon); the item gives no dated price level or forecast, so the period is set by the shared-quantity rule and is checked against the contract-price releases published during 2027.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract prices for the memory used in NVIDIA's AI racks — LPDDR5X DRAM/HBM and 3D NAND — be up in the fourth quarter of 2026 versus a year earlier, given the DRAM/NAND/HBM supply squeeze the item describes?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Reported contract price change (Q4 2026 versus Q4 2025, in percent or $/unit) for the DRAM/LPDDR5X, HBM and NAND going into AI racks, as published in memory contract price data.\",\n  \"period\": \"Q4 2026, settled by that quarter's contract price data; the item (published 2026-07-06) describes costs for the second half of 2026 and beyond but gives no release date, so the check date is set to the Q4 2026 contract price publication.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"question\": \"What will the year-over-year change in contract prices for server DRAM (DDR5/LPDDR5X) and 3D NAND be in calendar 2026, and therefore the memory content cost of Nvidia's Vera Rubin racks (about $2 million per rack, 25–30% of the bill of materials)?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The direction and size of 2026 contract price changes for server DRAM and NAND, which set the memory portion of Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack bill of materials and hence system pricing and cost per rack.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 — set by the item, which reports contract DDR5 prices already climbing sharply as of July 2026 and memory content up 435% generation-over-generation; measured at TrendForce's monthly contract price releases through December 2026.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"question\": \"Will contract prices for AI-server memory (DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory) rise in calendar 2026, and by how much?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The direction and magnitude of change in contract prices for DRAM/NAND/HBM (including DDR5 and HBM4) over calendar 2026.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026, per the item's reference to memory pricing and rack budgeting for the second half of 2026 and beyond.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract prices for the DRAM/LPDDR5X and NAND memory used in AI data-center racks rise in calendar 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The calendar-2026 change in industry contract prices for DDR5/LPDDR5X DRAM and NAND flash, the memory content that now makes up roughly 25–30% of an NVIDIA Vera Rubin rack's bill of materials (about $2 million per rack).\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar year 2026, measured by the Q4 2026 industry contract price data (TrendForce/DRAMeXchange series); the item (published 2026-07-06) gives no release date, so the calendar-year contract price series' release fixes the check date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract prices for AI-grade memory (DDR5 DRAM, HBM and NAND) rise in calendar 2026, as memory becomes a quarter or more of the cost of an AI rack?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The year-on-year change in contract prices for DDR5 DRAM, HBM and NAND in calendar 2026, as reported by memory-market price trackers and the memory makers' own price and bit-shipment disclosures.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 contract prices, settled by Q4 2026 contract-price releases and memory makers' Q4 2026 results (published around early 2027).\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"question\": \"What will the average contract price of DRAM memory (DDR5/LPDDR5X and HBM) used in AI data-center racks be in calendar 2027, relative to the sharp climb reported in 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The 2027 average contract price of DRAM/LPDDR5X (and NAND) memory used in AI racks, measured against the sharp increase reported for 2026.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 — set by the item: it says memory supply is tight and costs rising 'for the second half of 2026 and beyond,' so next calendar year is 2027.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"question\": \"Will contract prices for DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory keep rising through the second half of 2026, sustaining the roughly 435% jump in memory content per Nvidia Vera Rubin rack (about $2 million, 25–30% of the rack bill of materials) — the shared input cost that shapes Nvidia's rack pricing, hyperscaler AI budgets and memory availability for the VR200 ramp?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The level and direction of memory (DRAM/NAND/HBM) contract prices in H2 2026, and whether memory content per Vera Rubin rack stays near $2 million with availability sufficient for the Q4 2026 volume ramp.\",\n  \"period\": \"Second half of 2026 (item dated 2026-07-06; the item says buyers must budget for the second half of 2026 and beyond), checked against Q3 and Q4 2026 memory contract-price releases.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"question\": \"How tight will DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory supply be, and where will 2026 contract memory prices settle — the shared input whose cost Morgan Stanley estimates jumped 435% to about $2 million per Nvidia Vera Rubin VR200 rack and which the item says is raising component costs across the market?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"2026 contract memory prices and memory supply tightness, measured against Morgan Stanley's ~$2 million memory content per Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack (up 435% from the prior generation, 25-30% of the bill of materials) and reports of sharply higher contract DDR5 pricing.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 — set by the item: the VR200 generation ships from Q3 2026 with volume ramping in Q4, and the item describes the current DRAM/NAND/HBM squeeze as raising costs into 'upcoming products' and over the 'next two years' of capacity planning.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract prices for the memory used in NVIDIA's AI racks (LPDDR5X/HBM DRAM and 3D NAND) rise in calendar 2026, given AI-driven demand and constrained memory supply?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The full-year 2026 change in contract memory prices (DRAM/LPDDR5X/NAND) that NVIDIA's racks depend on, as measured by market contract-price indices, versus the sharp increases already described in the item.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar year 2026, settled by TrendForce's 2026 DRAM/NAND contract-price series (and memory makers' contract-pricing disclosures) covering the full year.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"question\": \"How high will contract memory prices — contract DDR5 DRAM and the AI-grade LPDDR5X/HBM that go into Nvidia's rack systems — run in the second half of calendar 2026, relative to mid-2026 levels?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The level of contract DRAM/NAND (DDR5, LPDDR5X, HBM) prices in H2 2026 versus mid-2026, the input-cost base for Nvidia's AI rack systems.\",\n  \"period\": \"Second half of calendar 2026 — set by the reason: the item reports contract DDR5 pricing climbing sharply in mid-2026 under constrained DRAM/NAND/HBM supply without naming a release date, so the check falls on Q3/Q4 2026 contract-price data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"question\": \"What will contract prices for the memory used in Nvidia's AI racks (LPDDR5X/HBM DRAM and 3D NAND) be in calendar 2027, after memory rose to 25–30% of the Vera Rubin rack bill of materials (about $2 million per rack, up 435%)?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Reported contract price levels and year-over-year changes for DDR5/LPDDR5X, HBM and NAND used in AI racks in 2027 versus 2026, and whether tight memory supply persists.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 (with 2H 2026 as the reported starting point) — set by the item: it calls memory cost a budget variable for the second half of 2026 'and beyond' and for 'the next two years'; a shared quantity takes next calendar year.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"question\": \"What will contract prices for AI-server memory (LPDDR5X/DRAM and 3D NAND) average in calendar 2027, the input cost embedded in Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack pricing and in hyperscaler AI budgets?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The level of contract memory prices in calendar 2027 versus 2026, as reported by contract-price trackers and memory makers' disclosed ASPs.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 (the 'next year' relative to the item's 2026 date; the item notes planners are budgeting capacity 'for the next two years'); set by the shared-quantity rule — settled when TrendForce/DRAMeXchange publish 2027 contract prices and memory makers report 2027 ASPs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"question\": \"What will contract prices for server DRAM (including DDR5) do over calendar 2026 — the memory input cost that now makes up 25–30% of the bill of materials of Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The change in contract DRAM/DDR5 prices through calendar 2026, and therefore Nvidia's per-rack memory cost and the price it can charge for a Vera Rubin system.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 (the item, dated 6 July 2026, reports contract DDR5 pricing already climbing sharply in 2026); checked against contract-price releases through Q4 2026 and the memory makers' December-quarter (Q4 2026) results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"question\": \"Where will DRAM/NAND (including DDR5, LPDDR5X and HBM) contract prices move over calendar 2026–2027 as AI data-center demand competes with device makers for constrained memory supply?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Direction and level of contract DRAM/NAND (incl. DDR5, LPDDR5X and HBM) prices over 2H2026–2027 relative to mid-2026, as reported in quarterly contract price data.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 (second half) through 2027, checked against quarterly TrendForce/DRAMeXchange DRAM, DDR5 and NAND contract price releases; set from the item's 2026-07-06 date and its 'second half of 2026 and beyond' framing, as the item gives no explicit price-release date or forecast figure.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"question\": \"What will happen to calendar-2026 contract prices for the memory that now makes up 25–30% of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin rack bill of materials — LPDDR5X/DRAM, 3D NAND and HBM — with supply reported tight against AI-driven demand?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The direction and magnitude of 2026 contract price changes for DRAM/LPDDR5X, NAND and HBM, and whether tight memory supply constrains Vera Rubin rack builds.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026, settled by memory contract price releases and memory makers' quarterly results through Q4 2026 (the item gives no date; the shared quantity takes the release dates of the 2026 price series).\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract prices for AI-grade memory (DRAM/DDR5, 3D NAND, HBM) rise in calendar 2026, given that memory is now 25–30% of a Vera Rubin rack's bill of materials?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The change in contract DRAM/DDR5, NAND and HBM pricing through calendar 2026, versus prior-year levels, as reported in market contract-price data and memory makers' results.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar year 2026, tracked from the item's 2026-07-06 publication through the Q4 2026 contract-price releases and memory makers' Q4 2026 results (reported early 2027).\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"question\": \"Will memory (DRAM, NAND and HBM) contract prices keep climbing through 2027 and tighten availability of the LPDDR5X/3D NAND/HBM content in NVIDIA's AI racks, raising system costs or limiting rack shipments?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The trajectory of memory contract prices and memory availability in 2026-2027, and whether memory content (now ~25-30% of the Vera Rubin VR200 rack bill of materials) becomes a binding cost or scheduling constraint for NVIDIA's AI rack shipments.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026-2027 — set because the item reports memory costs already up 435% per rack with rack volume ramping in Q4 2026 and organizations planning capacity for the next two years; next year's contract prices to be confirmed by contract-price releases.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract prices for the DRAM (including LPDDR5X/HBM) and NAND memory used in NVIDIA's rack-scale AI systems rise in calendar 2026, given constrained memory supply against AI-driven demand?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The 2026 change in contract prices for DRAM/LPDDR5X/HBM and NAND memory versus 2025, as reported by memory price trackers and by memory makers' own pricing disclosures; the item reports a 435% jump in memory content per Vera Rubin rack and that contract DDR5 pricing has climbed sharply, but gives no price level or percentage change.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 — the year the item (published 2026-07-06) describes as under memory supply constraint; settled by contract price releases through Q4 2026 and memory makers' quarterly results (reported early 2027).\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"question\": \"Will contract prices for DRAM (DDR5/LPDDR5X) and NAND keep rising through calendar 2027, pushing the memory content cost of an AI rack above the roughly $2 million Morgan Stanley estimates for a Vera Rubin NVL72 rack?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The direction and size of contract DRAM/NAND price changes in calendar 2027 and the resulting memory cost per high-end AI rack.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 — the item gives no year for memory pricing, so the period is set to the next full calendar year beyond the item's stated budgeting horizon of the second half of 2026 and beyond.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract prices for server DRAM (DDR5/LPDDR5X) and NAND change over calendar 2027, the memory market that now sets 25-30% of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin rack bill of materials?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The change in contract prices for server DRAM and NAND over calendar 2027, measured from contract-price tracking data, and whether the shortage-driven increases reported in mid-2026 continue or reverse.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027, the next calendar year after the item's 2026-07-06 publication, tracked through quarterly contract-price releases through Q4 2027.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"question\": \"What will contract prices for LPDDR5X and 3D NAND memory used in AI server racks be in calendar 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The direction and magnitude of LPDDR5X/3D NAND contract price changes in calendar 2026, as reflected in memory content cost per AI rack.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026, with Q4 2026 as the check point when Vera Rubin volume ramps; set by the item's Q3/Q4 2026 shipment schedule.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract prices for server memory — DDR5/LPDDR5X DRAM, high-bandwidth memory and 3D NAND — rise in calendar 2026, the memory that now makes up 25–30% of the bill of materials of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin VR200 rack?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Reported calendar-2026 contract price change for DDR5/LPDDR5X DRAM, HBM and 3D NAND, and whether memory content of roughly $2 million per VR200 rack (up 435% on the prior generation) holds or climbs further.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar year 2026, settled by 2026 contract price data through December 2026 (monthly DRAM/NAND contract price releases).\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract prices for DRAM memory used in AI data-center racks, including DDR5 and LPDDR5X, rise in calendar 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The direction and magnitude of DRAM contract-price changes in calendar 2026, as reported in TrendForce/DRAMeXchange contract-price data.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026; based on the item's discussion of AI infrastructure budgeting for H2 2026 and beyond and current contract DDR5 price increases, with the outcome settled by 2026 contract-price releases.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract prices for server memory — DRAM (DDR5/LPDDR5X), 3D NAND and high-bandwidth memory — rise in calendar 2026, the input that now makes up 25–30% of an NVIDIA Vera Rubin VR200 rack's bill of materials?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The change in contract prices for server DRAM, NAND and HBM in calendar 2026 (e.g. TrendForce quarterly DRAM/NAND contract price moves for Q3 and Q4 2026).\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 (Q3 and Q4 2026 contract prices); the item gives no figure or date for memory pricing, so the period is set from its focus on budgeting AI infrastructure for the second half of 2026 and beyond, and is settled by the quarterly contract-price releases.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract prices for AI-server memory — DDR5/LPDDR5X DRAM and 3D NAND used in NVIDIA's AI racks — rise in calendar 2026, given that memory is now a quarter-plus of rack cost and is flagged as constrained against AI-driven demand?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The calendar-2026 contract-price change for DDR5/LPDDR5X DRAM and 3D NAND, an input cost that bears on NVIDIA's rack pricing and product cost and on how far hyperscaler capex goes.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar year 2026, settled by Q4 2026 contract-price releases from TrendForce/DRAMeXchange (published early 2027); the item (published 2026-07-06) reports the increase is already under way but gives no figure or release date of its own.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract DDR5 memory prices change over calendar 2026, given the AI-driven memory supply squeeze that is raising component costs across the market?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The direction and magnitude of the change in contract DDR5 memory prices over calendar 2026.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar year 2026, settled by TrendForce/DRAMeXchange contract price releases through year-end 2026.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract DRAM/NAND prices — chiefly contract DDR5, alongside the LPDDR5X and HBM that go into AI racks — rise in calendar 2026, the memory input cost now embedded in every Nvidia Vera Rubin rack and in device makers' products?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The calendar-2026 change in contract DRAM contract prices (contract DDR5 and related LPDDR5X/HBM/NAND pricing) as reported by contract-price trackers.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar year 2026 — the item (published 2026-07-06) reports contract DDR5 pricing already climbing sharply during 2026; settled by contract-price releases through Q4 2026.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract prices for AI-server memory — DRAM/LPDDR5X, 3D NAND and high-bandwidth memory — rise in calendar 2026, given that memory now accounts for roughly a quarter of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin rack bill of materials?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Direction and magnitude of 2026 contract memory prices versus the prior year, and whether tight DRAM/NAND/HBM supply constrains AI rack builds.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar year 2026 — the item gives no release date, so the period is set to the calendar year it discusses for AI-infrastructure budgeting, settled by Q4 2026 contract memory price reports.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"question\": \"What will contract prices for the DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory used in NVIDIA's AI racks do over the next two years, and hence what will the memory content cost of a Vera Rubin-class rack be?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Contract memory pricing (and the resulting per-rack memory content cost) for AI rack builds versus the ~$2 million per rack Morgan Stanley estimates for the VR200 generation, and the effect of procurement structure on final rack pricing.\",\n  \"period\": \"Second half of 2026 through calendar 2027, the budgeting horizon the item addresses ('the next two years'); the item gives no release date, so it is settled by the contract memory price releases covering that window.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"question\": \"How far will DRAM, NAND and HBM memory content cost in Nvidia's AI rack systems go in calendar 2027 — i.e., what happens to memory contract prices and to per-rack memory content (about $2 million per Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack in 2026, up 435%, and 25-30% of the bill of materials) given constrained DRAM/NAND/HBM supply against AI-driven demand?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The 2027 memory content cost per Nvidia AI rack and the direction of DRAM/NAND/HBM contract prices, measured against the ~$2 million per VR200 rack (25-30% of a ~$7.8 million bill of materials) reported for 2026.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 contract pricing — set by the item's 'second half of 2026 and beyond' horizon and the shared-quantity rule (this or next calendar year).\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 32,\n  \"question\": \"What will average contract prices for DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory be in calendar 2026, as AI-driven demand runs against constrained memory supply?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The direction and magnitude of memory (DRAM/NAND/HBM) contract prices in 2026 versus 2025, and whether tight supply keeps raising AI-rack component costs.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 — set by the item: memory supply is described as tight and contract DDR5 pricing as having climbed sharply in an article dated 6 July 2026.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 33,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract DDR5 memory prices rise in calendar 2026, the memory-market price pressure the item ties to AI infrastructure and Nvidia's rack costs?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The change in contract DDR5 memory prices over calendar 2026.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026; set by the shared-quantity rule (this calendar year), to be settled by 2026 contract DDR5 price releases.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 34,\n  \"question\": \"What will contract prices for AI-relevant memory — DDR5/LPDDR5X DRAM, 3D NAND and HBM — average in calendar 2027, and will the memory content of a top-end Nvidia AI rack stay near the ~$2 million Morgan Stanley estimates for the Vera Rubin VR200 generation?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Calendar 2027 average contract price levels for DDR5/LPDDR5X DRAM, NAND and HBM, and the resulting memory dollars per rack in Nvidia's top AI system, measured against Morgan Stanley's ~$2 million per VR200 rack (435% above the prior generation).\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 — set by the reason: this is a shared price for the next calendar year after the item (dated 6 July 2026), the horizon over which the article says buyers are budgeting AI infrastructure.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 35,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract memory prices (DRAM/DDR5, 3D NAND and HBM) rise over calendar 2026, given AI-driven demand against constrained supply?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The 2026 change in contract memory prices — the cost line that has become 25–30% of Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack bill of materials and a strategic budget variable across the AI buildout.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 (Q4 2026 contract pricing) — set by the item, which reports contract DDR5 pricing has already 'climbed sharply' as of mid-2026 and that memory is 25–30% of the VR200 rack bill of materials for the second half of 2026 and beyond.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 36,\n  \"question\": \"What will contract prices for DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory be in calendar 2026, given AI-driven demand and constrained supply that the item says is now driving up memory content cost in AI systems?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The level and direction of 2026 contract DRAM/NAND/HBM prices (e.g., DDR5 contract prices), measured against the 435% generation-on-generation jump in memory content cost per Nvidia Vera Rubin rack and the memory share of the bill of materials rising to 25–30%.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 — set by the item: memory supply constraints and rising contract DDR5 prices are described as current in an article dated 6 July 2026 and affecting AI systems through 2026.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 37,\n  \"question\": \"How much will AI-server memory (DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory) contract prices rise over calendar 2026–2027, given memory now makes up 25–30% of Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack cost and is in tight supply?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The trajectory of DRAM/NAND/HBM contract prices for AI-server memory in calendar 2026–2027.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026–2027 (the VR200 ramp and the next-two-years AI buildout the item describes); set by the shared-quantity reason.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 38,\n  \"question\": \"What will contract prices for AI-relevant memory (DDR5/DRAM, LPDDR5X, 3D NAND and HBM) do over calendar 2026, the input cost that now makes up roughly a quarter to 30% of Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack bill of materials?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The direction and magnitude of 2026 memory contract pricing (DRAM/DDR5, LPDDR5X, 3D NAND, HBM) after the reported 435% jump in memory content per Nvidia AI rack, and whether memory inflation continues or eases.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026, with emphasis on H2 2026 — set because the item frames AI infrastructure budgeting for the second half of 2026 and beyond, reports memory supply tight and contract DDR5 pricing climbing sharply, and gives no specific release date of its own.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 39,\n  \"question\": \"What will average contract prices for data-center memory (DRAM, NAND and HBM) be in calendar 2027, given the AI-driven demand and tight supply the item describes?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Calendar-2027 average contract prices for DRAM, NAND and HBM, measured against the sharp 2026 increases reported in the item (which push memory to 25–30% of a Vera Rubin rack's bill of materials).\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 (next calendar year from the July 2026 item), checked against 2026 levels at quarterly memory contract-price releases through 2027.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 40,\n  \"question\": \"What will contract prices for the DRAM/LPDDR5X and NAND memory used in AI racks average in calendar 2027 versus 2026, and how tight will memory supply be relative to AI-driven demand?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The direction and scale of 2027 contract memory prices (DRAM/LPDDR5X and NAND) versus 2026, and reported evidence of whether memory availability is constraining AI rack output.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 — next calendar year, set by the reason (a shared price/quantity for this or next calendar year, from an item dated 6 July 2026).\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 41,\n  \"question\": \"What will contract prices for DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory be in calendar 2026, as AI-driven demand and tight supply raise memory costs that make up 25–30% of Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack bill of materials?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The level and direction of 2026 contract memory prices (DRAM/NAND/HBM), and whether the memory cost surge that Morgan Stanley estimates at about $2 million per Vera Rubin rack continues or reverses.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 — set by the item's 2H2026 Vera Rubin launch and its report that contract DDR5 pricing has climbed sharply; no specific release date is given in the item.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 42,\n  \"question\": \"What will contract memory prices — DRAM/LPDDR5X, 3D NAND and high-bandwidth memory — be over calendar 2027, given constrained supply against AI data-center demand and memory's rise to 25–30% of Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack bill of materials?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The level of contract DRAM (incl. LPDDR5X), NAND and HBM prices in calendar 2027 versus 2026, and whether the supply squeeze behind the memory cost increase persists or eases.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 — set by the reason: the item (dated 6 July 2026) describes the memory cost shift for the second half of 2026 and beyond and the constrained supply behind it, so the next full calendar year is 2027.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 43,\n  \"question\": \"What will DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory (HBM) contract prices be for AI infrastructure in calendar 2027, given the AI-driven memory supply squeeze that has pushed memory to 25-30% of the cost of Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack and sharply raised contract DDR5 pricing?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The 2027 average contract price level for DRAM/NAND/HBM (and the resulting memory content cost per AI rack), measured against the 435% jump in memory content per Vera Rubin VR200 rack and the sharply higher contract DDR5 pricing the item reports for 2026.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 - next calendar year relative to the item's 2026-07-06 publication; the item frames the memory squeeze for 'the second half of 2026 and beyond' into the Rubin ramp.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 44,\n  \"question\": \"How much will contract prices for AI-relevant memory (DDR5/DRAM, LPDDR5X, 3D NAND, HBM) rise in calendar 2026 — the input cost embedded in NVIDIA's AI racks and in other device makers' products?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The 2026 change in contract memory prices versus the prior year, as reported by memory-market price trackers.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026, settled by quarterly contract memory-price reports during 2026 (no explicit release date in the item; set to the calendar year the item discusses).\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 45,\n  \"question\": \"What will contract prices for AI-relevant memory (DDR5/LPDDR5X, NAND and HBM) do in calendar 2026 — rise further or ease — the input cost on which NVIDIA's Vera Rubin rack economics and other device makers depend?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The direction and level of contract DRAM/DDR5/LPDDR5X, NAND and HBM prices in calendar 2026 versus prior levels, as reported by memory-price trackers and memory makers.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 (the 'this year' from the item's 2026 date), when memory-price trackers and memory makers report contract pricing.\"\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
